1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,537
Houston, we've had a problem.

2
00:00:01,667 --> 00:00:04,595
Three men are breathing poison. The fix is a square peg.

3
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:08,061
An oxygen tank exploded on April 13, 1970.

4
00:00:08,167 --> 00:00:12,477
Lovell, Swigert and Haise ran into the lunar module, Aquarius.

5
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:15,574
Aquarius was built to keep two men alive for about two days.

6
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:18,012
Now it had to keep three men alive for four.

7
00:00:18,133 --> 00:00:20,721
Carbon dioxide from their breathing began to build up.

8
00:00:20,833 --> 00:00:23,069
The command module's filters were round.

9
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:24,877
The slot in Aquarius was square.

10
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,164
The filters would not fit.

11
00:00:26,267 --> 00:00:29,581
Engineers on the ground had one job: build an adapter from what was on board.

12
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:35,427
Plastic bags. Duct tape. Cardboard. A spacesuit hose.

13
00:00:35,533 --> 00:00:38,692
The crew built it step by step, while the air got worse.

14
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:42,293
The carbon dioxide dropped. They came home on April 17.

15
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:45,039
The mission never landed on the Moon. The crew came home.

16
00:00:45,167 --> 00:00:47,643
Would you have trusted a cardboard fix to keep you alive?
